cff-version: 1.2.0
message: >-
  If you use this work, please cite the paper below. Corrections and
  suggestions are welcome at the contact address given.
title: >-
  Quality per Gigabyte: Measuring Qwen3.8-27B Under 4 Bits on a 12 GB
  Consumer GPU
type: software
authors:
  - name: "Mericanii"
    given-names: "Yugendren"
    affiliation: "Mericanii (independent research lab)"
    email: 19thkingisreal@gmail.com
date-released: 2026-08-31
version: "v1.0-draft"
license: Apache-2.0
# url / repository-code: intentionally omitted until the repo is public.
# Fill in with the real repo URL before launch (see pub/STRUCTURE.md).
abstract: >-
  Independent quality-versus-size measurements of sub-4-bit GGUF builds of
  Qwen3.8-27B on a single RTX 3060 12GB, using llama.cpp and the full
  164-task HumanEval benchmark. Reports a quality/size curve with confidence
  intervals and paired significance tests, speculative-decoding ablations,
  a pre-registered negative result on best-of-n sampling at low bit-width,
  and a corrected mechanism claim for decode bandwidth by quant format.
keywords:
  - quantization
  - GGUF
  - llama.cpp
  - Qwen
  - HumanEval
  - consumer GPU
  - speculative decoding
  - inference optimization
contact:
  - name: "Mericanii (Yugendren)"
    email: 19thkingisreal@gmail.com
